# Custom SELinux policy patch, auto-loaded by Magisk/KernelSU at every boot.
#
# Some devices' base policy denies apps from connecting to the Zygisk
# companion socket (hosted in the zygote process's security context) even
# though Zygisk itself is active and working. This shows up as:
#
#   avc: denied { connectto } ... scontext=u:r:untrusted_app:... \
#        tcontext=u:r:zygote:s0 tclass=unix_stream_socket
#
# for every app process, regardless of which module is trying to use the
# companion API - not something specific to this module's code. These
# rules explicitly allow that connection for the app domains that
# actually need it.

allow untrusted_app zygote unix_stream_socket connectto
allow priv_app zygote unix_stream_socket connectto
allow system_app zygote unix_stream_socket connectto
allow platform_app zygote unix_stream_socket connectto
allow gmscore_app zygote unix_stream_socket connectto
allow shell zygote unix_stream_socket connectto
